<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <RootNamespace>StatsTid.Tools.DemoSeed</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>StatsTid.Tools.DemoSeed</AssemblyName>

    <!-- This is an OFFLINE demo-data generator, NOT a security surface:
         CA5394 — System.Random with a FIXED seed is the deterministic-output requirement
                  (same seed ⇒ byte-identical dataset). A crypto RNG would defeat the
                  entire reproducibility contract. No security decision rides on these draws.
         CA2100 — every SQL string in this tool is a STATIC literal (no user input); the
                  only parameterised values flow through NpgsqlCommand parameters.
         CA5351 — MD5 here is a DETERMINISTIC ID derivation (S97 enhed_id from the
                  organisation|name key), NOT a security primitive. A stable hash is required
                  so the user_enheder FK resolves to the same enhed_id; no secret is hashed. -->
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CA5394;CA2100;CA5351</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- S84 / TASK-8401 + TASK-8403: deterministic demo-data generator + API loader.
       The generator is pure C#; the loader drives the live API over HttpClient; the
       optional post-load verification uses Npgsql directly. Same Npgsql version as
       Infrastructure (8.0.3) to avoid transitive drift. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Npgsql" Version="8.0.3" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- S142 / TASK-14210 — THE S84 "SELF-CONTAINED: no production project references" CONTRACT
       IS RETIRED, by owner ruling OQ-10 (2026-09-16). It held from S84 until that ruling; the
       claim is deleted rather than left to rot, because a comment still promising self-
       containment would be a worse defect than the coupling it used to describe.

       WHAT IS REFERENCED: exactly ONE type — StatsTid.SharedKernel.Calendar.CopenhagenBusinessDate,
       the shared "which calendar day is it in Copenhagen?" helper (DST-correct: CET in winter,
       CEST in summer). SharedKernel has ZERO package and project references of its own, so this
       adds no transitive footprint. Precedent for a tools/ -> src/ edge: tools/ProjectionBackfill
       (S27 / TASK-2705) already references SharedKernel + Infrastructure.

       WHY THE RULING: StatsTid derives BUSINESS dates from the Danish calendar day, not the UTC
       one (the S142 sprint theme; instants such as created_at stay UTC). Both of this tool's
       wall-clock readings used to be correct only BECAUSE OF A FACT ABOUT THE MACHINE RUNNING
       IT — DateTime.Today is the machine-LOCAL day, which on a Danish developer's laptop already
       IS the Copenhagen day. A site that is correct for a reason nobody wrote down breaks the
       first time the reason changes: here, the first time anyone runs the reseed on a UTC CI box.
       The reference makes the Danish day EXPLICIT instead of circumstantially true.

       WHY THE DETERMINISM GUARANTEE SURVIVES (the contract this tool exists to keep: same seed +
       scale + reference-date => byte-identical output). The committed artifact
       docker/postgres/99-demo-seed.sql and the golden-legacy pin
       (tests/StatsTid.Tests.DemoSeed/GoldenLegacyPinTests.cs) are generated at the PINNED CONSTANT
       ReferenceDateResolver.PinnedDefault (2026-06-15) and therefore NEVER TRAVERSE THE CLOCK PATH
       AT ALL — no clock, Copenhagen or otherwise, can move them. Only the opt-in
       `reference-date rolling` branch reaches the helper, and that branch is non-deterministic BY
       DESIGN (it tracks the calendar so the local demo never goes stale) and is explicitly excluded
       from the pin. The generator itself stays wall-clock-free: every date it emits derives from the
       reference date it is handed. See README.md "Determinism". -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\SharedKernel\StatsTid.SharedKernel\StatsTid.SharedKernel.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- S114 / TASK-11400: the DemoSeed test suite constructs INTERNAL ScaleConfig/TreeProfile
       instances directly — (a) the golden-legacy pin rebuilds TODAY's no-override smoke config
       to prove override-absence is the byte-exact legacy path, and (b) the generation-time
       depth-assertion RED case needs a config that CANNOT reach manager depth 4. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="StatsTid.Tests.DemoSeed" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
